isha"'::jsonb, '"Kalpa, Chandas, Nirukta, Jyotisha, Shiksha, Vyakarana"'::jsonb, '"Vyakarana, Shiksha, Jyotisha, Chandas, Kalpa, Nirukta"'::jsonb, '"Nirukta, Jyotisha, Chandas, Vyakarana, Kalpa, Shiksha"'::jsonb, '"It extrapolates from one example to a universal historical claim without sufficient evidence"'::jsonb, '"It defines geometry too precisely"'::jsonb, '"It cites the number system"'::jsonb, '"It distinguishes source and interpretation"'::jsonb, '"Explain the stated relationship between Sanskrit and natural language processing"'::jsonb, '"Claim that all software must be written in Sanskrit"'::jsonb, '"Replace language analysis with a calendar chart"'::jsonb, '"Discuss only the mechanical keyboard"'::jsonb, '"Organize them as separate technology themes and compare each practice using relevant evidence and constraints"'::jsonb, '"Treat them as one identical process"'::jsonb, '"Put all evidence under the four Vedas"'::jsonb, '"Classify every theme as an Ashrama"'::jsonb, '"Nakshatrara Gyaan and agriculture; forest management and urban planning"'::jsonb, '"Only Vedic pronunciation and metre"'::jsonb, '"Only algebraic identities"'::jsonb, '"Only word-processing margins"'::jsonb, '"Purusharthas"'::jsonb, '"Vedangas"'::jsonb, '"Computer ports"'::jsonb, '"Forms of HTML"'::jsonb, '"Brahmacharya is the student stage and conventionally comes first; Vanaprastha follows Grihastha"'::jsonb, '"Brahmacharya is a Veda"'::jsonb, '"Vanaprastha is the goal of liberation"'::jsonb, '"The two terms refer to identical measurement units"'::jsonb, '"The Vedas form a core corpus; Puranas are described as encyclopaedic; Itihasa is a source of wisdom"'::jsonb, '"All three are names of Vedangas"'::jsonb, '"Puranas are CSS properties"'::jsonb, '"Itihasa is a unit of distance"'::jsonb, '"Find source evidence specific to that site before making the claim"'::jsonb, '"Assume the outline proves it for every site"'::jsonb, '"Use the title of the unit as the sole evidence"'::jsonb, '"Replace evi